quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  8,46,"And obey Allah and His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him), and do not dispute (among yourselves), for then you will lose heart, and your power will be gone. And be patient; indeed, Allah is with the patient."
  8,47,"And be not like those (pagans) who left their homes boastfully, only to be seen by people and to bar (other people) from Allah’s path. And Allah comprehends whatever they do."
  8,48,"And (remember) when Satan made their deeds fair-seeming to them and said: ‘No one among humankind shall overcome you today, and I am indeed your protector.’ But when the two troops saw each other, he withdrew upon his heels, saying: ‘Indeed I disown you. Surely, I see what you do not see. Truly, I fear Allah, and Allah is Severe in retribution.’"
  8,49,"And (remember) when the hypocrites and those possessing sickness in their hearts said: ‘Their Religion has deceived them.’ But whoever trusts in Allah, Allah is indeed All-Mighty, All-Wise."
  8,50,"If only you could see when the angels take away the souls of the disbelievers, striking their faces and their backs, saying: ‘Taste the punishment of the burning (of Hell)."
  8,51,"That is for what your hands have sent forth, and because Allah is never unjust to (His) servants.’"
  8,52,"(They are) like the people of Pharaoh and those before them, who denied Allah’s signs. So Allah seized them for their sins. Indeed, Allah is Strong (and) Severe in retribution."
